{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1362702-planning-a-one-shot-and-i-m-stumped","id":1362702,"title":"Planning a one-shot and I'm stumped.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-22T12:19:02-08:00","id":1362702,"title":"Planning a one-shot and I'm stumped.","content":"As I said before, I'm planning a one-shot with the potential of becoming a full series. The one-shot will be set in New Orleans on Ash Wednesday, and will begin as a procedural about a serial killer sacrificing people to odin. his latest victim is a member of one of the players' entourages. So far, so good.<br /> <br /> But there's a bait-n-switch. Scene one is the murder mystery and introduces 2 or 3 characters. Then I switch gears, and ask the rest of the table what they're doing. Let them wonder what's coming for them, and just when they think they got a handle on the story I'm going to hit the city with a Tsunami.<br /> <br /> And here's where I'm stuck. I need to come up with a couple of seven scenes that allow the players to be heroes during a major disaster aaaand I'm coming to a blank. anyone got any ideas. <br /> <br /> in case it's important, the Tsunami is the result of God Fall, specifically Triton, the son of Poseidon and the messenger of the sea has come to New Orleans in the flesh, so to speak. The Tidal wave is a side effect. It won't come up in the one shot, nor will they capture the serial killer. If the game becomes a regular those will be future plot-points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T13:36:57-08:00","id":1362716,"title":"","content":"Well from a narrative standpoint I question the satisfaction of having a one-shot where the stated premise is kind of dropped at the wayside and then left as a cliffhanger for if the campaign ever continues. That's kind of unsatisfying. Why not have it just be a murder mystery where the players are tracking things down, and it becomes increasingly obvious that the mystical is involved somehow?<br /> <br /> Or if you want to you can just open with &quot;It's a wonderful day in New Orleans except for the terrible tidal wave&quot; and in that case you can turn the aftermath into a Complex Action of sorts.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, do X things that aid in recovery efforts. You can use Path Connections and the like to help with these!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T18:37:07-08:00","id":1362774,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry, I wasn't clear. The players created characters and asked me to run a one shot, They have no preconception of what the game is going to be except that its going to be set in New Orleans. The player concepts are: <br /> <br /> A US Marshall with a past <br /> An Instagram Model and Influencer<br /> An Ever-Loving Therapist<br /> A Tech Magnate<br /> A Teacher's Pet and<br /> A Punk Kid <br /> <br /> They're pretty much relying on Fate to bring them together. I figure I'd have a little fun with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T20:58:14-08:00","id":1362792,"title":"","content":"Well yeah, it's just that you say the initial thing is &quot;So I'm going to set up a murder mystery&quot;, yes?<br /> <br /> But then you say the murder mystery won't be resolved in the one-shot? That feels a bit unsatisfying to me to read about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-22T23:21:29-08:00","id":1362802,"title":"","content":"I tend to agree...if the murder mystery is the point of the one-shot, it should be resolved in it. The tsunami, Godfall, Poseidon, those should be hooks for any future campaign. But resolve the one-shot in the one-shot, since that's your stated reason for the episode in the first place.<br /> Of course, nothing says there can't be a connection between the serial killer and a group who are opposed to Poseidon and his faithful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T00:19:46-08:00","id":1362812,"title":"","content":"Or heck, if the Disaster Relief is the major pull, say &quot;You were in New Orleans for Reasons when suddenly TIDAL WAVE&quot; and make it about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T06:26:38-08:00","id":1362868,"title":"","content":"Gnomish, your idea looks very similar to Actual Play of Terrible Trio from Onyx Pathcast - plot is about Poseidon in Miami, but events sound a lot as what you look for. \ud83d\ude0e I love Onyx Pathcast | Episode 54: Scion Actual Play Part One, let's play it!<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-z8xx4-b2b365\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://d2bwo9zemjwxh5.cloudfront.net/ep-logo/pbblog2761479/reduced_onyx_pathcast_final_curved_1200x628.jpg?s=6ef26b7b276daa77f3b2234d8d703a61&amp;e=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-z8xx4-b2b365\" target=\"_blank\"> Episode 54: Scion Actual Play Part One </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-z8xx4-b2b365\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.podbean.com/ea/pb-z8xx4-b2b365 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Episode 54: Scion Actual Play Part OneIn which Matthew, Dixie, and Eddy play Scion and discuss Cliffhanger (with Sylvester Stallone)! * Introductions* Reginald Pewty, Call of Cthulhu Anorak* Scion: Origin Actual Play* Cliffhanger (the movie)* Dixie's Dark Eras 2 progress* Matthew's Shunned by the Moon and C20 Player's Guide progress* Pirates of Pugmire Kickstarter* Where to find us on social media Links:Dark Eras 2 Backerkit: https://chronicles-of-darkness-dark-eras-2.backerkit.com/hosted_preordersC20 Player's Guide: https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/274520/C20-Players-GuidePirates of Pugmire Kickstarter: http://kck.st/2EoRkyp </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-23T07:12:36-08:00","id":1362878,"title":"","content":"Is it an Origin game or Hero ?<br /> Im asking because this will greatly influence how much the character can solve in one game session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":